            "decision_refs": [],
            "reactions": [
              {
                "emoji": "+1",
                "count": 2
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "msg_id": "M5",
            "speaker_id": 478887,
            "reply_to": "M3",
            "text": "Good point, @9197. The site's existing BMS uses Modbus TCP. I'll update that section to be explicit. Thanks for catching it.",
            "mentions": [
              9197
            ],
            "artifact_refs": [],
            "decision_refs": [],
            "reactions": []
          },
          {
            "msg_id": "M6",
            "speaker_id": 478887,
            "reply_to": "M4",
            "text": "Completely agree, @523835. That brings us to the pilot's success criteria. I propose we add an appendix to A1 defining these key performance metrics. For SoC accuracy, how about 'within +/- 2% of lab-measured value under defined load profiles'?",
            "mentions": [
              523835
            ],
            "artifact_refs": [
              "A1"
            ],
            "decision_refs": [],
            "reactions": []
          },
          {
            "msg_id": "M7",
            "speaker_id": 523835,
            "reply_to": "M6",
            "text": "That's a solid, verifiable target. I'm good with that. We should also define criteria for data availability (e.g., >99% uptime) and alarm response time.",
            "mentions": [],
