        "thread_goal": "Define and refine the laboratory test plan and validation approach.",
        "messages": [
          {
            "msg_id": "M19",
            "speaker_id": 478747,
            "reply_to": null,
            "text": "Hi all, as a follow-up to our requirements alignment, I've created the first draft of the Laboratory Test Plan (A2). It outlines the test matrix for temperature, load profiles, and some basic fault scenarios as per T2. Feedback is welcome.",
            "mentions": [
              478887,
              9197,
              523835,
              11752
            ],
            "artifact_refs": [
              "A2",
              "T2"
            ],
            "decision_refs": [],
            "reactions": []
          },
          {
            "msg_id": "M20",
            "speaker_id": 523835,
            "reply_to": "M19",
            "text": "Thanks for the quick turnaround. I've reviewed the plan. The load profiles are good, but the fault scenarios section is a bit light. We need to explicitly test for sensor failure (open circuit, short circuit) and communication loss. These are common failure modes in the field.",
            "mentions": [],
            "artifact_refs": [],
            "decision_refs": [],
            "reactions": [
              {
                "emoji": "bulb",
                "count": 1
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "msg_id": "M21",
            "speaker_id": 9197,
            "reply_to": "M19",
            "text": "I agree with @523835. Also, we need to add specific lab safety procedures. For example, defining the required PPE, emergency stop procedures, and having a fire extinguisher nearby. This needs to be explicit before we can get safety officer approval.",
            "mentions": [
              523835
            ],
            "artifact_refs": [],
            "decision_refs": [],
            "reactions": [
              {
                "emoji": "+1",
                "count": 1
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "msg_id": "M22",
            "speaker_id": 478887,
            "reply_to": "M20",
            "text": "Excellent points. The goal of T3 is to catch these issues before we go to the field. Let's also add a test case for algorithm recovery after a power cycle of the monitoring unit. We need to ensure it re-initializes correctly.",
            "mentions": [],
            "artifact_refs": [
              "T3"
            ],
            "decision_refs": [],
            "reactions": []
          },
          {
            "msg_id": "M23",
            "speaker_id": 478747,
            "reply_to": "M21",
            "text": "All great feedback. I'll add a dedicated 'Safety Procedures' section and expand the fault scenario matrix to include sensor failures, comms loss, and power cycling. I'll also set up the Issue Tracking Log (A7) so we can start logging findings from the lab tests.",
            "mentions": [],
